From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-raphael: front camera power + probe node

The stock camera DT labels `qcom,cam-sensor@2` with CAMF_RESET/CAMF_VDIG_EN, so
the front module sits on CSIPHY1, CCI0 master 0 (i2c-3), MCLK2 = tlmm gpio15,
reset = tlmm gpio12 and its VDIG enable = tlmm gpio95, with viodd + BOB + S8 +
L17 as supplies.

Add the missing fixed regulator for the gpio95 enable and a probe node on the
first CCI bus so the sensor can be powered and identified from userspace.  The
node borrows a known driver only to run a power sequence; `keep_power=1` leaves
the rails and MCLK up so the real address can be found by scanning, exactly the
method that located the tele OV8856 at 0x36.

Deliberately no `regulator-always-on` anywhere: the camera rails must only be up
while a driver/user asks for them (see the two boot bricks caused by the PMIC
rails).

Not tested yet - it was written while the phone was wedged after the async-link
experiment of round 19.

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@
 	camera_vdig_tele: regulator-camera-vdig-tele {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "camera_vdig_tele";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <1352000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1352000>;
 		enable-active-high;
 		gpio = <&tlmm 93 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		vin-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
 	};
+
+	/* front module VDIG enable, stock DT CAMF_VDIG_EN */
+	camera_vdig_front: regulator-camera-vdig-front {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "camera_vdig_front";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		gpio = <&tlmm 95 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		vin-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
+	};
@@ i2c-bus@0 {
 		i2c-bus@0 {
 			reg = <0>;
+
+			/* front module: CSIPHY1, MCLK2 gpio15, reset gpio12,
+			 * VDIG_EN gpio95.  Address is a placeholder until the
+			 * scan finds the real one. */
+			camera_front: camera@10 {
+				compatible = "ovti,ov8856";
+				reg = <0x10>;
+				reset-gpios = <&tlmm 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+				clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_MCLK2_CLK>;
+				clock-names = "xvclk";
+				assigned-clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_MCLK2_CLK>;
+				assigned-clock-rates = <19200000>;
+				avdd-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
+				dovdd-supply = <&camera_viodd_ldo>;
+				dvdd-supply = <&camera_vdig_front>;
+				vl17-supply = <&vreg_l17a_3p0>;
+				status = "okay";
+			};
